      "writtenOn": "2025-01-02T19:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You changed the tests to be written in terms of `raa489000_tcpm_should_enter_bist_mode` and `tcpc_set_bist_mode`, but but those are functions that the driver should be calling. There isn\u0027t a `tcpc_get_message_raw`, so I think you should write the test in terms of `tcpc_config[port].drv-\u003eget_message_raw`. That will get you coverage of most of the lines you\u0027re missing right now.\n\nYou can see an example of setting this up in the [generic TCPCI driver test](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/drivers/default/src/tcpci_test_common.c;l\u003d523;drc\u003d665fbcfb1ea1378e5dafeaffa43fd809c961c0aa). You would replace the message header/contents in that test with the BIST message from this test.",
